# Naming and code style

Canonical: `docs/Personal_Rules.md` sections 7, 8, and 16.

| Item                  | Style                | Example                    |
| --------------------- | -------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Component files       | PascalCase           | `TaskCard.tsx`             |
| Utility files         | camelCase            | `formatDate.ts`            |
| Backend files         | Nest dot-separated   | `tasks.controller.ts`      |
| Type files            | [name].d.ts in types | `task.d.ts`                |
| Tables/columns        | snake_case           | `task_items`, `created_at` |
| Environment variables | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE     | `DB_HOST`                  |

- `frontend/src/types`, `backend/src/types`, and `desktop/src/types` hold shared/global types only. Props and one-off types stay in their consuming file.
- Feature-shared declarations live in `types/[module-name]/[name].d.ts`; cross-feature declarations in `types/common/[name].d.ts`.
- Each declaration file exports its types as a module. Import shared types; do not redeclare them.
- Classes stay where they belong: DTOs in `dtos`, entities in `models`.
- Frontend common static API contracts use `frontend/src/types/common/api.d.ts`; module-shared contracts use the feature type folder. Runtime `ApiError` belongs in `lib/api/client.ts` or `lib/api/errors.ts`, never a declaration file.
- Every component/controller starts with a block explaining purpose, responsibilities, usage, and its feature wiki page.
- Comment important functions/features and non-obvious behaviour, not trivial formatters or assignments.
- ESLint and Prettier check the code. One root Prettier configuration; frontend `eslint-config-next`, backend/desktop `typescript-eslint`, each with `eslint.config.mjs`.
- Lint and formatting must pass before merge. Disabled rules need reviewable reasons; no blanket top-of-file disable.

Example header:

```tsx
/**
 * Task summary card for the task list.
 * Renders title and status; used by TaskList.
 * Wiki: wiki/TaskBoard.md
 */
```

- Desktop runtime source is TypeScript compiled from desktop/src to desktop/dist. Node frontend entry points may use .mts. Keep build/test configs in their established tool-supported formats; do not edit compiled output.
